# Call with both positional and named arg for the same parameter
# Type checker can't detect this in same-dict letrec (TypeVar arm skips named-arg checks)
# Evaluator catches it as a missing-argument error at runtime
[f: [fn [let x@Int y@Int] [+ x y]]
 result: [f 42 x: 99]]
=== error
[E024] missing argument for required parameter 'y' (defined at 4:10-4:22)
  in [f ...] at 4:10-4:22
  in [f ...] at 4:10-4:22
